From 33f58ff0c1496ce6b36bacc5273a9a3aa429bf13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:42:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restore a reverted vote in canonical order

Reverting a Solar vote (2/2) now stores the sender's restored votes in
sortVotes order: percent descending, then name in byte order (patch
04). bootstrap and applyToSender already stored that order;
revertForSender stored the votes of the sender's previous vote
transaction in the order in which that transaction was signed.
Decoding does not check the key order of a vote asset, so any signer
can write {a9: 50, a10: 50}.

The order is consensus-visible. Wallet.calculateVoteAmount gives the
i-th remainder unit of a split balance to the i-th delegate in the
votes Map. A node that reverted a block kept a non-canonical Map, while
a node that never saw that block, or that rebuilt its state from
history, kept the canonical one. Every later balance change of that
wallet then credited the remainder units to different delegates, so
delegate.voteBalance, and with it the delegate ranking, could differ
between nodes. Example: balance 101, previous vote signed as
{a9: 50, a10: 50}: s1-ref-v1 restored a9 51 and a10 50, a node that
bootstrapped had a10 51 and a9 50. The same bug exists in Solar 4.3.1
(a previous vote signed as {a: 30, b: 70} restored a 31, b 70).

Every other write of the votes attribute was checked:
- solar/vote.ts bootstrap and applyToSender: already sortVotes order;
- core/vote.ts (1/3 legacy vote) bootstrap, apply and revert: the Map
  holds at most one entry, and 1/3 is inactive since patch 02;
- the Wallet constructor: an empty Map;
- state-loader.ts: restores the Map in the order state-saver.ts wrote
  it, which is canonical once every writer is. Not changed. A saved
  state written by an s1-ref-v1 node is not migrated; a devnet is
  started again from its genesis instead.
The pool's revert of a removed vote goes through the same method. The
previousVotes of the Vote event (API only) is unchanged.

Test: patches/tests/07-vote-revert-canonical-order.test.js, with real
Wallet objects and stub repositories. A previous vote signed as
{a9: 50, a10: 50} (it passes strict fromBytes in that order) is
restored as a10, a9 with a10 51 and a9 50; apply then revert returns
the votes Map and every delegate's voteBalance to their prior state;
the reverting node and a bootstrapping node get the same Map;
{a: 30, b: 70} is restored as b 71, a 30. It fails on s1-ref-v1 (7 of
12 checks) and on b45369d7, and passes with this patch.

Patch: 07
Consensus: yes
